## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Source and package version match the new tag and release notes.
- [x] The release waits for every parallel qualification lane.
- [x] The actual published archive, checksum file and manifest agree.
- [x] Manifest source identity equals the exact tagged commit.
- [x] Previous tags/releases/assets and all predecessor tracking are preserved.
- [x] No private continuity, applicant values or unrelated work is published.
- [x] No installation, independent-app control or live LinkedIn action occurs.

## Completion evidence
Publish source 7fbd525ad5f32b9b8f5e00e2c3bea4d496dc0601 with verified
Zanark author/committer identity and both session trailers, then normally push
its new annotated v0.2.5 tag. Main run 43115725352 and tag run 43116415970
pass all thirteen independent qualification lanes and the fail-closed barrier.
The tag run's subsequent publication succeeds; v0.2.5 is independently
verified as the latest release:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/releases/tag/v0.2.5
The release body equals the checked-in notes and has exactly the Windows ZIP,
manifest and SHA256SUMS assets. Verify both published checksums, all 454 ZIP
member sizes/hashes, exact manifest membership and tagged source identity.
Downloaded hosted reports confirm 1,082 passing cases per supported Python
version, separately from the earlier 1,081-case local full qualification.
All five prior complete release/asset records, original tag objects and forty
predecessor tracking records are preserved. Private context publication stays
skipped; the four reviewed public handoff files remain unchanged.
No installation, independent-app control, live LinkedIn action or human
acceptance is included. The unsigned package still does not bundle a browser.

